course: dictionary
lesson: 14533
title: Keep going: persevere
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To persevere means to keep trying to do something, even when it is difficult or you fail at first, and not give up. Look for the clue words: "even when" tell you the task is still hard, and the person keeps going anyway.
explain: «Maya got the maths sums wrong three times, but she persevered and got them all right in the end.» Three wrong tries, then a right answer: Maya did not stop after the mistakes. She kept trying, so persevered means kept trying.
explain: You can persevere with something, or persevere in doing it. «Tom persevered with his new violin piece, practising every day until it sounded right.» Similar words are keep going, stick at it and don't give up.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Maya kept trying and did not give up» still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: Persevere is a verb: persevere, perseveres, persevered, persevering.
fact: «Persevered» means kept trying even though it was hard.
fact: Persevere is often followed by "with" or "in": persevere with a spelling list, persevere in learning to swim.
fact: Perseverance is the noun: it is the quality of not giving up.
fact: Similar words: keep going, stick at it, don't give up.
exercise: «Ella found the puzzle hard, but she persevered until she solved it.» What does persevered mean? | Asked someone else to do it | Lost the puzzle pieces | Gave up and went to bed | *Kept trying even though it was hard
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to persevere? | Sleep | Forget | Stop | *Stick at it
exercise: Mr Patel says, «Keep persevering with your spellings, and they will get easier.» What does persevering mean here? | Writing the spellings in red | *Carrying on trying, even when it is hard | Copying a friend's spellings | Stopping your spellings for the day
test: «Sam persevered with his bike, falling off many times before he could ride it.» What does Sam do? | Stops riding for ever | Sells his bike after one fall | *Keeps trying after failing | Waits for someone else to teach him
test: Which sentence shows someone persevering? | *Lily read the hard page again, slowly, until she understood it | They decided to skip the project | He stopped halfway through the race | She threw her book down and said it was too hard
exam: Which choice best shows what persevere means? | *Kept going with a hard task, even after failing | Gave up as soon as it felt difficult | Laughed at the mistake and forgot the task | Waited for someone else to finish
